gomodel:6ab067da00000385
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "Built by claude4go 2026-09-23 from Rizzo et al 2021 EMBO J (PMID:33749896): GOLPH3 binds the LxxR cytosolic tails of B4GALT5, A4GALT, ST3GAL5 and ST8SIA1 and recycles them in COPI vesicles from the trans cisterna (cryo-IEM, RUSH), retaining them in the Golgi and preventing lysosomal degradation; GOLPH3 KD/OE lowers/raises LacCer, Gb3, GM3 output. Cargo adaptor MF also from Welch et al 2021 (PMID:34473204). PI4KB (1-phosphatidylinositol 4-kinase activity) directly positively regulates GOLPH3 by generating the trans-Golgi PI4P pool that recruits it (Dippold 2009 PMID:19837035; PI4KIIIbeta named as the kinase by Rizzo 2021); per project convention the kinase reaction itself (PI -> PI4P) is not described. GOLPH3->client edges are 'indirectly positively regulates' (IMP): GOLPH3 controls client localisation and level, not catalysis. Trans-cisterna location is direct (IDA) for B4GALT5 only; inferred (IC) for the three co-clients and for the lumenal location of GlcCer/LacCer/Gb3/GM3/GD3 (with Lannert 1998 PMID:9446606). Downstream Gb3->Akt/mTOR mitogenic signalling deliberately left out (mechanism unresolved)." , "2026-10-20: PI4KB activity unit removed (no paper shows PI4KB acting on GOLPH3; link rested on inhibitor/yeast data). Replaced by PI4P (CHEBI:58178) 'is small molecule activator of' GOLPH3 cargo adaptor activity (IMP: Golgi PI4P depletion and PI4P-binding mutants, PMID:19837035; R90L and PIK93, PMID:42276998), PI4P located in GO:0160288 (IC)." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. GOLPH3, a COPI cargo adaptor recruited by PI4P, retains the glycosphingolipid synthases B4GALT5, A4GALT, ST3GAL5 and ST8SIA1 in the trans-Golgi, controlling LacCer, Gb3, GM3 and GD3 synthesis (Rizzo 2021)." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "development" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8769-177X" ;
        dc:date                "2026-10-20" ;
        dc:title               "GOLPH3-dependent intra-Golgi recycling of glycosphingolipid synthases (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00000385 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

